Revision history of WwW-GenGenLib-Template-Provider


0.00_00  2026-11-10  RC
    (Based on nginx and Neocities providers; this too is
     mostly written by Claude... but what else is new eh.)

    + RdKw::WwW::GenGenLib::Template::Provider: a Template
      Toolkit provider that names files as the locale does
      (to_fs of GenGenLib 0.0100), and knows what the source
      declares in its header, and what those declare in
      theirs (walk_deps):
        ALLOW_DEPS (on): what is declared may be loaded, even
          by a name ABSOLUTE or RELATIVE would refuse;
        CHECK_DEPS (off): only what is declared may be;
        RELATIVE_DEPS, ABSOLUTE_DEPS (off): whether what is
          declared may climb out (..) of its root, or be
          absolute without one;
        CHECK_HAVE (off): the source must HAVE itself
          (siteconf checks that already).
      What a template is given is taken as it is, and
      compared with the declarations after canonpath.
      A ${U+...} in a declaration is a character, not a
      variable, and RELATIVE_DEPS and ABSOLUTE_DEPS look at
      what it spells: ${U+002E}${U+002E}/ is ../ to them.

    + Messages say what is wrong (undeclared dependency:
      `file'), and not how to fix it; and name a file as a
      header would too, after it, if one of the PREFIXES
      leads there: `site/x' (${a}/x), escaped so that it is
      one name in a header.  (Borrowed from Neocities code!)

    + PREFIXES: those symbolic prefixes (by default ${a},
      ${B}/${b} and ${B}/${c}).  The longest expansion wins;
      then the shortest prefix, then the first in order.
